# Secrets for the clean watchers, sourced by watch-movie.sh / watch-tv.sh.
#
# Copy to .env in this directory (gitignored) and fill in. Do NOT put secrets in
# the .plist files here: those are tracked in git.
#
# launchd does not read login shell profiles, so exporting these in ~/.zprofile
# works for an interactive run and is invisible to the watchers under launchd.
#
# TMDB v3 API key. Enables --lookup, which resolves a year for releases whose
# filename has none ("The.End.of.Oak.Street.2160p...mkv"). Without it those
# files are reported as "SKIP (unparsed media)" and never filed.
TMDB_API_KEY=

# Plex token. Enables the post-run rescan: after a commit run, CleanMedia asks
# Plex to scan just the directories it touched, instead of waiting for Plex to
# notice. Plex's own auto-update is unreliable on an external volume, which is
# why renames sometimes show up immediately and sometimes not until the hourly
# scheduled scan. Without this the notification is a no-op and nothing changes.
#
# Find it: Plex web UI > any item > ... > Get Info > View XML, then copy the
# X-Plex-Token value out of the URL. Or read it locally:
#   defaults read com.plexapp.plexmediaserver PlexOnlineToken
PLEX_TOKEN=
# Defaults are fine unless Plex is not on this machine.
# PLEX_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:32400
